{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Data Security and Data Integrity ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to read and write about data security and data integrity", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Review of the Simple Past Tense of the Verb Be ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the simple past to express an action in the past that takes place once, never or several times. It can also be used for actions taking place one after another or in the middle of another action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In the first chart  you can see the structure. Remember verb BE does not use an auxiliary verb, it uses <strong>Was</strong> and<strong> Were.</strong><br/><br/>  Don't forget to use  was and were depending on the subject and the singular or plural form of the sentence.<br/><br/>  Simple past tense uses time expression like:<br/> <strong>Yesterday</strong><br/> 2 minutes <strong>ago</strong><br/> <strong>In</strong> 1990<br/> The other day<br/> <strong>Last</strong> Friday<br/><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Interrogative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Data integrity <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was</span> associated with data security.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Data integrity <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was not</span> associated with data security.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Was</span> data integrity associated with data security?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Data security, as well as data integrity, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">were </span>  important few years ago.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Data security, as well as data integrity, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">were not</span> important few years ago.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Were</span> data security and data integrity  important few years ago?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "They didn't know what the topic was about.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Companies hired businesses to help them to have their data protected in order to satisfy the customer needs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Data security, as well as data integrity, were not important a few years ago. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Infinitives of Purpose with \u201cIn Order To\u201d", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>\u201cIn order to\u201d</strong> is a subordinating conjunction. Subordinating conjunctions are adverb phrases that create a grammatical connection between two clauses, making one dependent on the other. They must come at the beginning of the clause (sentence).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <strong>\u201cIn order to\u201d</strong> with an infinitive form (to + verb) to express the purpose of something.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">We all need motivation <strong>in order to</strong> achieve and do our best work. </span><br/><br/> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How to write meaningful sentences in order to explain the concept of data security and data integrity: a simple formula to follow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Companies hire businesses to help them to have their data protected in order to satisfy the customer needs.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "How to Improve Your Writing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to write a letter, an invitation, an essay, a business email or a blog you are looking to do it in a clear and organize way. Improving your writing is as easy as these tips:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "1. Lead with your main idea, in other words write your main idea at the beginning.<br/>  2. Vary the length of your sentences, if it is an explanation use a long sentence, but if it is an idea, you can use a short one.<br/> 3. Put key words to emphasize at the beginning or end of a sentence.<br/> 4. Vary sentence types and structures, so you can use some questions or commands in your writing.<br/> 5. Use active verbs, the idea is not to abuse the passive voice or the use of verb be.<br/> 6. Use specific nouns and verbs that really show what you mean.<br/> 7. Cut the clutter, otherwise you will end up with unnecessary words. 8. Read aloud when you revise.<br/> 9. Actively edit and proofread your final draft before sending or handing over your writing.<br/> 10. Use a dictionary.<br/>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "audience ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "group of people who read or listen to your speech", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: First, you need to understand your audience.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "broad ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something wide, open or clear", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For instance, data security and data integrity are two broad concepts that come from database administration. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sensitive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something highly delicate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Data security, regarding databases, is the form to ensure sensitive data, this consist of the assignment and control of users' level of access.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "diversion ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that turns aside from its course or purpose", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Moreover, it is the use of monitoring tools to detect a compromise, diversion, or unauthorized change to database files. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stolen", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when someone takes other's property without permission", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Data integrity is associated with data security since the completeness and accuracy of data can be compromised, stolen or damaged. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "staff ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of workers or assistants ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Within the database structure itself, data administrators and the staff maintain the links between data fields and a locking system.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about Data Security and Data Integrity differences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a brochure in which you explain the importance of these two concepts for the database administration.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your brochure with your classmates and compare your ideas.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I research about Data Security and Data Integrity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a brochure to explain the importance of these concepts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I show my brochure to my classmates and discuss with them about database administration and these concepts.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can read and write about data security and data integrity.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can read and analyze information related to data security and data integrity.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write meaningful sentences to explain a concept.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "How important is data for an organization?", "type": "Free Heade